Z||000000||FieroGT||08-26-99||09:23 AM||||I just read the post that concerned the wiring for the alternator. Now I have some questions for the collective knowledge of the board. <p>My other fiero ('85 SE-V6) has has charging problems for about 1 1/2 yrs. now. <p>Symptoms: Sometimes it will charge very low (11V), and sometimes it will charge very high (17V). When I run the car during the day, no problem. At night, when there is a significant electrical drain like headlights, blower motor on high, or wipers, the car seems to miss, and sometimes stall. When I give it heavy throttle around 2000RPM it misses and cuts out and the tach jumps all over the place. Sometimes it even stalls when the fron fan comes on, but starts right back up. <p>Things I've replaced: Battery, alternator, plugs, wires, cap, rotor, ignition module, ignition coil, both battery cables, and checked all grounds, including the ground strap from the chassis to the motor. The only things not replaced are the pickup coil (doubt it's that) and the wiring. My wiring in the car looks old and beat. When I have the low charging problem, if I jiggle some wires it -may- correct itself for a little while. I tried examining the wiring, but I think I'll have to remove the harness for that. I was thinking about rewiring the alternator and regulator plug, because it's about all I can do. Any suggestions? Or a spare harness for a V6-4spd car for cheap?<br>
Z||000001||FieroGT||08-26-99||07:42 PM||||HELP! Did anyone see my post?<p>Thanks, guys (& girls!).<p>
Z||000002||DJRice||08-27-99||07:53 AM||||I would double check the connection at that distribution block near the battery.  Make sure everything there is clean and tight.<p>Otherwise, you may have a wiring problem.  However, there could be a problem with one of the components that you run at night that causes extra current drain.  Maybe fan motor dying or something.<p>Also, you may check the your alternator belt.  If it is old and hasnt been changed, it could be streched enought not to drive your alternator like it should.  It wouldnt necessarily do a bunch of sqealing if it was loose.<p>Good luck
